  "description": "We wish to reinstate a stud wall in our house. The wall used to be there many years ago but was knocked down to create one bed with a large kitchen/dining room.\nWe have recently purchased the flat and wish to convert it back to a two bed. We want to put the stud wall back up to recreate the second bedroom.\nWhen the wall goes back up it will mean the only access to the garden is via the new bedroom. This mean we wish to create a second exit to the garden via the kitchen window.\nWe also have some cracks on the front exterior of the property. From surveys these are not structural cracks but just cosmetic. There are around 6 small cracks that we wish to have filled and then repaint the house the same colour that it is currently.\nAfter speaking with the planning portal phone line, waltham forest building regulations and Charlotte Cartwright (Conservation Officer Waltham Forest council) we have been told we need planning permission for the repair and painting of the front of the house and also the exit door to the garden via the current kitchen window. For the stud wall we have been told to get complete building regulations. \n",
  "subdivision_of_building": "- Putting up a stud wall to create the second bedroom only affects the ground floor.\n- Creating the doorway to the garden via the kitchen only affects the rear ground floor.\n- Filling the cracks in the render and repainting the house affects the front exterior of the house.",
